{"id":"n-20261013-o3512v","category":"business","display_title":"Global Markets Diverge Amid Semiconductor Selloff","display_title_he":"השווקים הגלובליים מתפצלים ברקע מפולת במניות השבבים","short_summary":"European shares advanced despite hefty impairment charges at energy giant BP, while Asian equities tumbled following an aggressive retreat across semiconductor stocks.","english_level":"C1","words":424,"reading_time":3,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Graphs_showing_the_wealth_distribution%2C_1900-2014.png/960px-Graphs_showing_the_wealth_distribution%2C_1900-2014.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"Esteban Ortiz-Ospina · CC BY 4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Graphs_showing_the_wealth_distribution,_1900-2014.png"},"sources":[{"name":"Globes","domain":"globes.co.il","url":"https://www.globes.co.il/news/article.aspx?did=1001559284","title":"אירופה פותחת בירוק למרות מחיקות הענק של BP; הקוספי ננעל בצניחה","published_at":"2026-10-13T07:28:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-13T07:28:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-13T07:47:20.762Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["International equity markets presented a stark study in contrasts on Tuesday morning, as European bourses pushed into positive territory while Asian exchanges endured severe turbulence driven by a sharp retreat in technology shares. The pan-European Stoxx 600 advanced by 0.4 percent, buoyed by the British FTSE 100, which led regional momentum with a 0.9 percent climb. Germany's DAX and France's CAC 40 added 0.2 percent and 0.4 percent respectively. Corporate headlines centered on British energy behemoth BP, which unveiled a profit warning disclosing that its third-quarter accounts would include substantial post-tax write-downs spanning between 3 billion and 4.5 billion dollars. The company clarified that these impairments predominantly stem from its energy transition and low-carbon operations, noting that they would be excluded from underlying replacement cost profits ahead of full financial disclosures scheduled for October 30. Meanwhile, the euro recovered modest ground against the dollar, rising about 0.3 percent to 1.118 dollars, though analysts at Dutch lender ING cautioned that lingering anxieties regarding French fiscal stability could restrain the currency's trajectory into next year, estimating a range between 1.10 and 1.15 dollars.","The cautious optimism across European trading desks diverged markedly from the distress registered across Asian financial centers. South Korea experienced the sharpest downturn, where the benchmark Kospi index closed down by 5.5 percent after plunging over 5 percent and forcing authorities to activate an emergency 'Sidecar' mechanism to halt automated trading for five minutes. The selloff was spearheaded by high-profile semiconductor manufacturers: memory provider SK Hynix plummeted over 8 percent, while Samsung Electronics retreated by 7.9 percent. Japan’s equity markets succumbed to similar sentiment, with the Nikkei shedding 1.8 percent as tech-focused investment giant SoftBank tumbled roughly 8 percent, alongside steep declines among domestic equipment makers like Tokyo Electron and Renesas. Market observers linked the downturn to spillover effects from Wall Street, exacerbated by financing concerns raised by key semiconductor executives and mounting competitive pressure from Chinese firm CXMT, though analysts emphasized that South Korean chipmakers retain robust structural positions in advanced memory production.","Across the Atlantic, Wall Street futures painted an uneven portrait. Contracts linked to the technology-heavy Nasdaq lost 0.8 percent, while S&P 500 futures dipped 0.1 percent and Dow Jones contracts rose 0.5 percent ahead of quarterly earnings from premier banking institutions. Concurrently, commodity markets witnessed energy prices cooling from recent heights, with Brent crude dipping to 105.29 dollars per barrel and American benchmark WTI easing to 92.34 dollars. Oil prices continue to balance tight geopolitical conditions in the Middle East, surging freight charges, and depleted strategic reserves against political maneuvers aimed at stabilizing global supply chains. In contrast to the equities selloff, crypto markets displayed optimism as Bitcoin advanced 1.24 percent to trade around 83,652 dollars."],"facts":[{"fact":"European stock bourses opened higher, with the Stoxx 600 gaining 0.4%, the British FTSE rising 0.9%, the German DAX adding 0.2%, and the French CAC adding 0.4%.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Energy company BP issued a profit warning, stating its third-quarter results would feature post-tax write-downs of $3 billion to $4.5 billion tied to energy transition and low-carbon segments.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"South Korea's Kospi index triggered a five-minute 'Sidecar' mechanism to pause automated trading and closed down 5.5%, pressured by steep drops in SK Hynix and Samsung Electronics.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Japanese stocks declined, with the Nikkei losing 1.8% and tech conglomerate SoftBank sliding around 8%, alongside heavy losses among domestic chip equipment suppliers.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Brent crude settled around $105 per barrel and WTI traded near $92 per barrel following elevated geopolitical friction in the Middle East and strain on shipping routes.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Wall Street futures were mixed as investors awaited third-quarter earnings reports from major financial institutions including JPMorgan, Wells Fargo, Citigroup, and Goldman Sachs.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"International","lemma":"international","pos":"adj","he":"בינלאומי","name":"false"},{"text":"equity","lemma":"equity","pos":"n","he":"מניות","name":false},{"text":"markets","lemma":"market","pos":"n","he":"שוק","name":false},{"text":"presented","lemma":"presen